Fixed. The bug was in `src/import_merge.ts:7` — the match used an exact string comparison (`b.url === inc.url`), so URLs differing only in hostname case never matched and got added as duplicates.

**Change:** comparison now normalizes the hostname via the `URL` API (`new URL(url).hostname.toLowerCase()`), which is inherently case-insensitive for hostnames. Non-URL strings fall back to a plain lowercase comparison.

**Verified:**
- `deno check` passes; `deno test` — 3 passed, 0 failed.
- Direct run: `https://example.com/a` + `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` → 1 entry with unioned tags `["x","y"]`; a genuinely different URL still produces 2 entries.


